WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.480
Firebird Form

00:03.720 --> 00:05.750
What are you doing, Mr. Red?

00:05.750 --> 00:07.120
Can't you tell?

00:07.120 --> 00:09.080
I'm reorganizing the closet.

00:11.680 --> 00:14.730
What's this "Firebird Form" thing?

00:15.880 --> 00:17.990
You know how heroes tend to power-up somewhere midway through the series

00:17.990 --> 00:20.580
so they can fight even stronger enemies, right?

00:20.580 --> 00:21.860
That's basically what it is.

00:21.860 --> 00:25.160
Firebird Form is my ultimate form.

00:25.160 --> 00:26.650
There we go.

00:26.880 --> 00:32.520
You won't be able to use it right away if you put it so far back!

00:34.780 --> 00:36.510
Dodz,

00:37.380 --> 00:39.240
Homas.

00:39.880 --> 00:42.680
We will conquer this land

00:42.680 --> 00:45.270
as our first step towards world domination.

00:45.270 --> 00:47.170
In the city of Kawasaki,

00:47.170 --> 00:48.810
a normal city located in the Kanagawa Prefecture,

00:48.810 --> 00:52.480
a new era of fear and chaos is about to leave its mark.

02:29.170 --> 02:30.290
What the-

02:30.290 --> 02:31.750
Did you punks just get here too?

02:31.750 --> 02:32.770
No way.

02:32.770 --> 02:33.410
For reals?

02:33.410 --> 02:35.110
Then Master Vamp's been by himself all this time?

02:36.070 --> 02:37.400
We're so sorry, Master Vamp.

02:37.400 --> 02:38.870
Sorry we're late!

02:42.340 --> 02:44.450
He <i>was </i> all by himself!

02:44.450 --> 02:46.380
We're sorry, Master Vamp!

02:46.380 --> 02:48.020
We're sorry we couldn't get here at one o'clock.

02:48.020 --> 02:50.550
We're sorry for being irresponsible and not cleaning up as promised.

02:50.550 --> 02:53.210
I was resistance training outside with a wet towel,

02:53.210 --> 02:54.380
but my towel wore out.

02:54.680 --> 02:57.690
I had to cover some guy's shift at work because he didn't show up.

02:57.690 --> 03:00.890
I was trying to get Durtle to come, but I couldn't get a hold of him.

03:04.370 --> 03:06.060
Who are you people?

03:07.860 --> 03:09.960
He's angry!

03:09.960 --> 03:12.270
Master Vamp would never say something like that!

03:12.270 --> 03:15.040
I can just clean the entire base by myself, right?

03:15.040 --> 03:16.090
U-Um...

03:16.090 --> 03:19.240
I need to refill the bucket, so move.

03:20.270 --> 03:21.590
You reap what you sow.

03:21.590 --> 03:23.170
You guys should know better

03:23.170 --> 03:24.120
than to be so oblivious to the time.

03:24.120 --> 03:26.160
You guys should take more responsibilty as sensible adults!

03:26.160 --> 03:27.550
The nerve of this guy!

03:27.550 --> 03:29.140
You've got a lot of balls saying that!

03:29.140 --> 03:30.890
You're nothing but a freeloader!

03:30.890 --> 03:33.930
You should be helping Master Vamp clean!

03:33.930 --> 03:36.890
Go make up for it by cleaning up the base.

03:36.890 --> 03:39.100
He's right.

03:39.100 --> 03:42.000
Yeah, we have to cheer him up.

03:42.000 --> 03:44.450
We can't spend New Year's Eve like this.

03:44.450 --> 03:47.940
Showing up to New Year's breakfast would be really awkward if we don't.

03:47.940 --> 03:49.800
Let's do it guys.

03:51.450 --> 03:52.860
Clean the ceiling before the floor.

03:52.860 --> 03:55.120
The dust from the ceiling will fall on the floor if you do it after,

03:55.120 --> 03:56.720
and you'll just end up cleaning the same area twice.

03:56.720 --> 03:57.280
Yes, sir.

03:57.280 --> 04:00.000
Isn't it hard to move around in that armor?

04:00.000 --> 04:01.960
Why don't you change into something more comfortable?

04:04.170 --> 04:07.730
Oh dear, it's a shame the bedsheets aren't being dried while the sun's out.

04:07.730 --> 04:10.300
Geez you guys should really think things through.

04:10.300 --> 04:12.160
This is why Mr. Red beats us all the time.

04:12.560 --> 04:13.990
Master Vamp,

04:13.990 --> 04:15.190
where are you going?

04:15.190 --> 04:16.370
Shopping.

04:21.180 --> 04:23.830
Clean the ceiling before the floor.

04:23.830 --> 04:26.490
The dust from the ceiling will fall on the floor if you do it after,

04:26.490 --> 04:28.040
and you'll just end up cleaning the same area twice.

04:28.520 --> 04:30.480
Just forget about cleaning and go shopping for me.

04:30.480 --> 04:32.910
I wrote down everything we need.

04:32.910 --> 04:33.720
Okay.

04:33.720 --> 04:36.550
Try putting a little more thought into it next time.

04:39.710 --> 04:40.920
God damn.

04:40.920 --> 04:43.860
Give me a break, it's New Year's Eve.

04:44.730 --> 04:47.170
You're a Hero, aren't you?

04:48.570 --> 04:49.890
Who are you guys?

04:49.890 --> 04:51.780
My name is Devileye.

04:51.780 --> 04:55.510
We've come to Kawasaki in order to conquer the world.

04:56.080 --> 04:58.120
Wait, are you guys an evil organization?

04:59.950 --> 05:01.370
What if we are?

05:01.370 --> 05:03.680
"What if we are?"

05:03.680 --> 05:07.280
I believe the question was "are you guys an evil organization," punk bitch.

05:09.050 --> 05:10.540
Oh, that's right.

05:10.540 --> 05:12.500
We're an evil organization.

05:12.500 --> 05:14.570
Spike Cannon!

05:17.380 --> 05:20.330
Dodz has defeated three Heroes already,

05:20.330 --> 05:24.140
and our ambition tells me that you're going to be number four.

05:24.140 --> 05:26.650
Sorry, but I've got some shopping to do.

05:26.650 --> 05:28.260
Are you running away?

05:29.050 --> 05:30.540
Well actually,

05:30.540 --> 05:33.610
you guys should've done your research first before coming.

05:33.610 --> 05:36.630
There's already an evil organization called "Florsheim" here.

05:36.630 --> 05:37.440
What?

05:37.440 --> 05:39.120
Oh yeah,

05:39.120 --> 05:41.610
you guys should go defeat Florsheim first,

05:41.610 --> 05:43.520
and then come back to fight me when you're done.

05:43.520 --> 05:45.680
You guys would have to take them down anyway

05:45.680 --> 05:48.400
if you're going to conquer the world, right?

05:50.450 --> 05:51.880
Flor... shei-

05:51.880 --> 05:55.070
There's an evil organization called Florsheim, see?

05:55.070 --> 05:57.330
So go clean those guys out first.

05:57.330 --> 05:59.580
An evil organization called Florsheim?

05:59.580 --> 06:00.370
Like I said,

06:00.370 --> 06:03.630
I have to go shopping, so I can't fight you guys anytime soon,

06:03.630 --> 06:06.730
unless you actually want to wait for me while I buy kagami mochi.

06:06.730 --> 06:09.530
You could be getting further ahead

06:09.530 --> 06:12.280
if you took care of Florsheim during that time, right?

06:12.280 --> 06:14.360
Right?

06:14.360 --> 06:15.910
You're right, but...

06:15.910 --> 06:17.990
I'll show you where their base is.

06:17.990 --> 06:20.270
You know where Florsheim's base is?

06:20.270 --> 06:21.660
Why wouldn't I?

06:21.660 --> 06:24.760
Here, give me something to write with, so I can draw a map.

06:25.400 --> 06:27.400
Give me something to write with!

06:27.600 --> 06:28.780
Do we have anything?

06:28.780 --> 06:30.260
Homas should have something.

06:30.260 --> 06:30.960
Here you go.

06:30.960 --> 06:31.890
Thanks.

06:31.890 --> 06:34.800
It's not too far from here, so just ask someone if you can't find it.

06:34.800 --> 06:37.840
Pretty much everyone around here knows where they live.

06:37.840 --> 06:39.290
Here.

06:39.290 --> 06:40.310
See ya.

06:42.910 --> 06:46.520
There's nothing we can do about him if he has to go shopping.

06:46.520 --> 06:51.290
Then we'll just go defeat Florsheim before killing off the Hero!

06:51.290 --> 06:52.390
Yes, sir!

06:52.890 --> 06:54.310
Before we do that, Master Devileye.

06:54.310 --> 06:55.000
What is it?

06:55.000 --> 06:56.560
Aren't you hungry?

06:57.160 --> 06:58.120
I'm hungry.

06:58.120 --> 06:59.070
We should eat something.

06:59.770 --> 07:01.850
In that case, we shall eat something.

07:01.850 --> 07:06.740
It would be hard to fight especially when we have to move around on a full stomach.

07:06.740 --> 07:07.880
You have a point there.

07:07.880 --> 07:10.130
Then we won't eat.

07:10.130 --> 07:13.500
Why don't we split some bread from the convenience store, then?

07:13.500 --> 07:15.320
That'll probably be fine.

07:15.320 --> 07:16.420
All right.

07:16.420 --> 07:18.030
We shall do as you said!

07:18.030 --> 07:19.080
Yes, sir!

07:19.080 --> 07:20.100
Geez.

07:20.100 --> 07:23.900
And here I was thinking I'd make them some delicious soba for New Year's Eve.

07:23.900 --> 07:26.400
Those lazy bums.

07:27.160 --> 07:28.970
Monsters?

07:28.970 --> 07:32.630
They shouldn't be loitering in front of a convenience store like that!

07:32.630 --> 07:35.430
I can't let other people think that they're associated with us.

07:35.430 --> 07:37.100
I'll have to warn them.

07:40.960 --> 07:44.070
So you told those monsters to go attack Vamp?

07:44.070 --> 07:46.560
You <i>did </i> tell me to go shopping.

07:46.560 --> 07:49.620
But didn't you say that one monster defeated three heroes already?

07:49.620 --> 07:53.920
I think he meant serious business, judging by his punch.

07:53.920 --> 07:57.360
You're one of Florsheim's monsters, aren't you?

07:57.360 --> 08:00.090
Oh no, Vamp's in trouble!

08:00.090 --> 08:03.410
Vamp and his monsters are so weak that they can't even take you down, you know.

08:03.410 --> 08:05.260
What the hell are you saying?

08:05.260 --> 08:06.800
Finish him, Dodz.

08:10.580 --> 08:12.450
Armour Tiger!

08:12.450 --> 08:16.880
What the hell do you think you're doing to Master Vamp?

08:16.880 --> 08:17.920
What?

08:18.390 --> 08:20.350
They're not weak at all.

08:22.260 --> 08:24.430
I'm just too strong for them.

08:29.200 --> 08:32.860
I'm sorry I'm so worthless.

08:32.860 --> 08:33.860
I really am...

08:33.860 --> 08:36.240
I told you to watch your strength Armour Tiger.

08:36.240 --> 08:38.330
You're too strong for your own good.

08:38.330 --> 08:39.970
I'm so sorry.

08:39.970 --> 08:43.030
And you guys shouldn't be acting like high school delinquents either.

08:43.030 --> 08:46.060
Don't you know that loitering in front of the convenience store bothers other people?

08:46.060 --> 08:49.330
I can't have others thinking that you guys are part of our organization.

08:51.160 --> 08:52.900
You have a point there.

08:52.900 --> 08:54.000
I apologize.

08:56.410 --> 08:59.180
So why did you come here, Armour Tiger?

08:59.180 --> 09:04.630
We thought that New Year's Eve shopping could be stressful one way or another,

09:04.630 --> 09:08.970
and figured one of us should go to help lighten the load.

09:08.970 --> 09:10.800
I'm sorry!

09:12.110 --> 09:13.840
Hello!

09:13.840 --> 09:14.970
Kayoko!

09:14.970 --> 09:16.640
Hello, Geirus.

09:16.640 --> 09:17.870
Is Vamp here?

09:17.870 --> 09:20.200
Yes, he's in the kitchen right now.

09:20.200 --> 09:22.800
Thank goodness he's safe.

09:22.800 --> 09:24.500
Oh, it's nothing.

09:24.500 --> 09:26.450
Here you go, I made you guys some New Year's Soba.

09:26.450 --> 09:28.700
Thank you so much!

09:28.700 --> 09:30.750
Master Vamp, Master Vamp!

09:30.750 --> 09:31.770
Oh don't bother calling him.

09:31.770 --> 09:33.870
I have to hurry back anyway.

09:36.140 --> 09:40.640
Could you take some of this tempura over to Kayoko once they're done, Geirus?

09:40.640 --> 09:41.490
Yes, sir.

09:41.490 --> 09:45.060
Looks like he's in a better mood.

09:45.060 --> 09:47.190
That Kayoko sure is a lifesaver.

09:47.190 --> 09:48.070
Come on now,

09:48.070 --> 09:51.700
what am I going to do with three monsters idling around in the kitchen?

09:51.700 --> 09:52.670
Get to cleaning.

09:52.670 --> 09:53.570
Hello!

09:53.570 --> 09:55.710
Oh, looks like someone's here again.

09:56.310 --> 09:58.960
Oh, what's going on you guys?

09:58.960 --> 10:01.470
We've come to help with the cleaning.

10:01.470 --> 10:03.670
I won't be returning to Egypt this year.

10:03.670 --> 10:05.600
There's really nothing to do by myself in the apartment anyway.

10:05.600 --> 10:07.120
And so we thought:

10:07.120 --> 10:09.860
We're going to help clean the base!

10:09.860 --> 10:11.330
Washcloth, washcloth.

10:11.330 --> 10:13.390
Come in you guys,

10:13.390 --> 10:14.450
come in.

10:14.450 --> 10:16.060
So you punks are here.

10:16.060 --> 10:18.780
Let's all spend New Year's Eve together.

10:18.780 --> 10:20.260
Sounds good to me.

10:20.260 --> 10:21.470
Can we really?

10:21.470 --> 10:25.630
That's exactly why I brought my own New Year's Eve Soba cup noodles.

10:25.630 --> 10:27.480
Cup noodles on New Year's Eve too?

10:27.480 --> 10:29.750
His own Soba cup noodles!

10:42.170 --> 10:45.770
Happy New Year!

10:45.770 --> 10:47.620
Our objective this year is to be <i>wild</i>.

10:47.620 --> 10:50.400
The Kawasaki division this year will be <i>wild</i>.

10:50.400 --> 10:51.300
<i>Wild</i>!

10:52.630 --> 10:56.200
Why don't we go make New Year's wishes at the temple, Master Vamp?

10:56.200 --> 10:56.960
That's a good idea.

10:56.960 --> 10:58.160
We should go!

10:58.160 --> 10:59.230
Shall we?

10:59.230 --> 11:02.580
Let's go, Master Vamp!

11:05.140 --> 11:07.160
Let's go see what fortune we'll get for this year.

11:07.160 --> 11:10.550
I'll pass. I don't believe in those things.

11:10.550 --> 11:12.640
Mr. Red!

11:12.640 --> 11:13.270
Huh?

11:13.270 --> 11:14.520
This voice can only be...

11:14.520 --> 11:16.140
We're over here!

11:16.140 --> 11:17.830
Vamp!

11:17.830 --> 11:19.210
Happy New Year, Vamp.

11:19.210 --> 11:20.970
Happy New Year, Kayoko.

11:20.970 --> 11:22.560
Happy New Year, Mr. Red.

11:22.560 --> 11:24.280
Happy New Year!

11:24.280 --> 11:26.040
That's enough, shut up, you punks!

11:26.040 --> 11:27.610
Oh, Mr. Red?

11:27.610 --> 11:30.810
This year you shall taste hell for sure.

11:30.810 --> 11:31.880
You can count on it!

11:34.490 --> 11:34.950
Ow.

11:35.390 --> 11:36.650
Would you stop that?

11:36.650 --> 11:39.120
I'll kick your ass if you don't stop.

11:39.120 --> 11:41.950
He didn't have to change to "wild" mode so fast...

11:42.730 --> 11:44.670
I wonder if that girl's not cold wearing a miniskirt.

11:44.670 --> 11:46.110
You're wearing one too.

11:46.110 --> 11:47.130
You are too.

11:47.130 --> 11:47.800
Oh my.

11:48.100 --> 11:48.870
Hididlyho?

11:48.870 --> 11:52.370
Happy giggity New Year's!

11:52.370 --> 11:53.750
Isn't this Tanaka?

11:53.750 --> 11:55.840
So sorry, sorry.

11:57.210 --> 11:59.430
Let's go buy charms, Master Devileye.

11:59.430 --> 12:01.280
Yes, we should.

12:51.390 --> 12:53.020
Astro Fighter Sunred.

12:53.020 --> 12:55.950
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

12:55.950 --> 12:59.400
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.
